VeridianOS: ewmh: xcb_ewmh_init_atoms_replies() accepts a NULL cookie array

Completes 0003: xcb_ewmh_init_atoms() now returns NULL when an
allocation fails (as it already did for a connection without screens),
but xcb_ewmh_init_atoms_replies() indexed the cookie array unchecked, so
the documented xcb_ewmh_init_atoms_replies(ewmh, xcb_ewmh_init_atoms(c,
ewmh), e) sequence still crashed. It now returns 0 for a NULL array;
both return values are documented in the header. (Prepared for
upstream, gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/lib/libxcb-wm.)

--- a/ewmh/ewmh.c.m4
+++ b/ewmh/ewmh.c.m4
@@ -593,6 +593,10 @@
   uint8_t ret = 1;
   xcb_intern_atom_reply_t *reply;
 
+  /* xcb_ewmh_init_atoms() failed */
+  if(!ewmh_cookies)
+    return 0;
+
   for(atom_nbr = 0; atom_nbr < NB_EWMH_ATOMS + ewmh->nb_screens; atom_nbr++)
     if((reply = xcb_intern_atom_reply(ewmh->connection, ewmh_cookies[atom_nbr], e)))
       {
--- a/ewmh/xcb_ewmh.h.m4
+++ b/ewmh/xcb_ewmh.h.m4
@@ -358,7 +358,7 @@
  * @param c The connection to the X server
  * @param ewmh The information relative to EWMH
  * @param screen_nbr The screen number
- * @return The cookies corresponding to EWMH atoms
+ * @return The cookies corresponding to EWMH atoms, or NULL on failure
  */
 xcb_intern_atom_cookie_t *xcb_ewmh_init_atoms(xcb_connection_t *c,
                                               xcb_ewmh_connection_t *ewmh);
@@ -368,7 +368,8 @@
  * previously sent
  *
  * @param emwh The information relative to EWMH
- * @param ewmh_cookies The cookies corresponding to EWMH atoms
+ * @param ewmh_cookies The cookies corresponding to EWMH atoms (if NULL,
+ *        as returned by xcb_ewmh_init_atoms() on failure, 0 is returned)
  * @param e Error if any
  * @return Return 1 on success, 0 otherwise
  */
